# The sites of rules WS, WD, WE and WF (tests/check_test_waits.py) that a sweep
# has not moved onto the owner yet, counted per file: `file RULE=n ...`.
#   WS  a clock or a sleep of the row's own (time.sleep, time.time, ...)
#   WD  a product duration written as a literal name, not through
#       gui_owner.product_duration / product_option_line
#   WE  one read of the END of a session (not alive(), poll() is not None,
#       returncode is not None, exit_code()) where the row should wait with
#       WpeSession.ended_within; a "still running" check is not counted
#   WF  a sleep inside the text of a program or a stand-in script that a
#       debugger or a row runs, where the row should wait at a
#       tests/program_gate.py gate
# A count may only fall; a count above the measurement fails as stale.  The
# check prints the current list with --list.
